! The templates of `frames.xfst` against the words they go around, so the
! fixture needs typey-type and phrases as well: what a frame is shown is what
! another dictionary wrote. `artifacts` names them.
!
! `...` in the second column is a held stroke: its keys are read and the text
! they belong to is not written yet. The line after the word reports the frame,
! under its own outline.

! ---- templates
!buffer
STPR*T
HAOER
!buffer
STPHO*BT
HAOER
!buffer
SPHO*RPB
HAOER
!buffer
STPHAO*EURT
HAOER

! A brief whose only claim on the stroke was a `-T` fold. A fold is a last
! resort, so the frame comes first: this writes "either here or" and not
! "either here" plus "the".
!buffer
SAO*EURT
HAOER

! The word comes first, so the word took the capital. A frame with a word of its
! own moves it: ". From here to", not ". from Here to".
!buffer
TP-PL
STPR*T
HAOER

! Two words, which is what `next = 2` shows, and their own capitals stay.
!buffer
STPR*T
TPHORB
!buffer
STWAO*EPBD
-FT

! Three words is more than a frame is shown, so it does not fire and the phrase
! stands as it was written.
!buffer
STPR*T
PHO*RPB

! A pair writes punctuation only, so the capital stays on the word.
!buffer
TP-PL
SKWO*ET
HAOER
!buffer
SPR*EPB
HAOER
!buffer
SPWA*BGT
HAOER
